 "state_profile": {
  "voting_summary": "Florida splits its vote across early in-person (44% in 2024), mail (25%), and election day (22%). Polls close at 7 p.m. Eastern (8 p.m. in the Panhandle); pre-processed mail and early votes are released within minutes of the close, then election day precincts report, making Florida the fastest-counting big state, effectively complete by mid-evening. Mail must arrive by election day, with no postmark grace period. Mail ran D+18 while early and election day votes ran R+22 to R+24, so the first dump skews Democratic and the state reddens through the evening.",
